    "diagnosis": "Relative frequencies of primary tumours and of brain metastases derived from them",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Tumours with a high propensity to metastasize to the brain are lung cancer, breast cancer, renal cell carcinoma, and melanoma. In this series of brain metastases, about 14% of cases in male patients and 8% of cases in female patients were diagnosed as carcinoma of unknown primary (CUP) {22012135; 22212630}. Data are based on the histology of archival tissue samples: 874&nbsp;cases collected in 1990&ndash;2011 at the Institute of Neurology (Neuropathology), Medical University of Vienna. Metastases for which surgery was not performed are not represented. The relative frequencies of brain metastases may differ substantially in other regions of the world.",
    "source": "",
